1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,070
A question paper becomes an online test.

2
00:00:03,070 --> 00:00:05,310
Equations, typed in seconds.

3
00:00:05,310 --> 00:00:07,630
Students join from any phone.

4
00:00:07,630 --> 00:00:09,470
Cheating gets caught.

5
00:00:09,470 --> 00:00:12,430
And every result lands, ranked.

6
00:00:12,430 --> 00:00:16,190
This is TestoZa — and these are its top ten features,

7
00:00:16,190 --> 00:00:18,605
with exactly how to use each one.

8
00:00:19,705 --> 00:00:22,220
Number one: Generate with AI.

9
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:26,150
Got your question paper as a PDF, or just photos?

10
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:28,790
Open Generate with AI, choose the file —

11
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:31,510
a three-page PDF, answer key included —

12
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:33,459
and tap Extract Questions.

13
00:00:33,559 --> 00:00:34,439
Now watch.

14
00:00:34,439 --> 00:00:37,879
The AI reads every single page, and the questions

15
00:00:37,879 --> 00:00:40,679
start arriving one by one — options,

16
00:00:40,679 --> 00:00:42,519
maths, everything.

17
00:00:42,519 --> 00:00:45,421
In about half a minute, all twelve are done.

18
00:00:45,521 --> 00:00:48,081
It even read the answer key on the last page,

19
00:00:48,081 --> 00:00:50,561
so every answer is already marked.

20
00:00:50,561 --> 00:00:53,488
Have a quick look, save, and your paper is now a test.

21
00:00:54,053 --> 00:00:57,531
Number two: maths and science, typed properly.

22
00:00:58,341 --> 00:01:00,901
Open the test in the builder — all twelve questions

23
00:01:00,901 --> 00:01:01,941
are already here.

24
00:01:01,941 --> 00:01:04,741
Add a question, and type the words as usual.

25
00:01:04,741 --> 00:01:07,381
For the formula, open Maths and symbols —

26
00:01:07,381 --> 00:01:08,893
this is Sy Pad.

27
00:01:09,073 --> 00:01:13,153
Type h equals u t minus, tap the fraction key,

28
00:01:13,153 --> 00:01:17,793
one over two, then the power key, for t squared.

29
00:01:17,793 --> 00:01:20,513
A proper formula — no code to learn.

30
00:01:20,513 --> 00:01:23,533
Insert, and it sits right inside the question.

31
00:01:24,098 --> 00:01:27,173
Number three: type in Hindi — or any of a hundred

32
00:01:27,173 --> 00:01:28,643
and nineteen languages.

33
00:01:29,324 --> 00:01:31,643
Tap the language switch, pick Hindi,

34
00:01:31,643 --> 00:01:33,643
and just type in English letters.

35
00:01:33,643 --> 00:01:37,084
Every word turns into Hindi the moment you hit space

36
00:01:37,084 --> 00:01:38,843
no Hindi keyboard needed.

37
00:01:38,843 --> 00:01:40,923
Now the question is in both languages,

38
00:01:40,923 --> 00:01:43,039
and the options go in just like before.

39
00:01:43,577 --> 00:01:46,863
Number four: real exam patterns.

40
00:01:47,673 --> 00:01:50,313
Plus four, minus one, on every question.

41
00:01:50,313 --> 00:01:52,553
Need JEE Advanced style?

42
00:01:52,553 --> 00:01:56,233
Make it multiple correct, choose JEE Advanced partial

43
00:01:56,233 --> 00:01:58,309
marks, and mark the right answer.

44
00:01:58,409 --> 00:02:01,609
Now split the paper into sections, and give every

45
00:02:01,609 --> 00:02:04,809
section its own timer, the way SSC does.

46
00:02:04,809 --> 00:02:08,569
Split it anywhere: questions seven to thirteen become

47
00:02:08,569 --> 00:02:09,609
Section B.

48
00:02:09,609 --> 00:02:11,769
Ten minutes here, ten minutes there…

49
00:02:11,769 --> 00:02:12,552
save.

50
00:02:13,096 --> 00:02:15,576
Number five: go live in one click —

51
00:02:15,576 --> 00:02:17,700
inside an anti-cheating exam room.

52
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:21,420
When the test is ready, tap Conduct exam.

53
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:23,500
You get a secure exam link.

54
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:26,224
Start conducting, and the exam is live.

55
00:02:26,404 --> 00:02:28,484
TestoZa even tells you the next step:

56
00:02:28,484 --> 00:02:30,004
set up the exam room.

57
00:02:30,004 --> 00:02:31,364
Force full screen.

58
00:02:31,364 --> 00:02:34,084
Catch every tab or app switch, set a limit —

59
00:02:34,084 --> 00:02:36,964
say three warnings — and the test submits itself.

60
00:02:36,964 --> 00:02:40,071
Block copy-paste, right-click, and the back button.

61
00:02:40,171 --> 00:02:43,451
On the Results tab, you decide what candidates see

62
00:02:43,451 --> 00:02:44,731
after the exam.

63
00:02:44,731 --> 00:02:48,011
And shuffle the questions, so no two candidates get

64
00:02:48,011 --> 00:02:49,131
the same order.

65
00:02:49,131 --> 00:02:49,892
Save.

66
00:02:50,513 --> 00:02:52,776
Number six: share it anywhere.

67
00:02:53,456 --> 00:02:56,016
Next tip: send it to your candidates.

68
00:02:56,016 --> 00:02:58,416
Copy the link, or share it straight to your class

69
00:02:58,416 --> 00:02:59,456
WhatsApp group.

70
00:02:59,456 --> 00:03:00,656
No phones in class?

71
00:03:00,656 --> 00:03:01,936
Get a join code.

72
00:03:01,936 --> 00:03:02,816
Six digits.

73
00:03:02,816 --> 00:03:05,126
Write it on the board, and students type it at testoza

74
00:03:05,126 --> 00:03:07,255
dot com slash join.

75
00:03:07,810 --> 00:03:10,541
Number seven: collect the details you need.

76
00:03:11,271 --> 00:03:12,951
Name is asked by default.

77
00:03:12,951 --> 00:03:14,951
Add Roll Number, or anything else —

78
00:03:14,951 --> 00:03:16,951
batch, school, phone.

79
00:03:16,951 --> 00:03:19,170
Candidates fill it in before they start.

80
00:03:19,708 --> 00:03:22,508
Number eight: an exam room on any phone.

81
00:03:22,508 --> 00:03:24,266
No app, no sign-up.

82
00:03:24,946 --> 00:03:27,826
Here's a student on her phone, at testoza dot com

83
00:03:27,826 --> 00:03:28,866
slash join.

84
00:03:28,866 --> 00:03:31,986
She types the six digits, and her exam opens.

85
00:03:31,986 --> 00:03:34,263
Name, roll number, start.

86
00:03:34,363 --> 00:03:37,083
Full screen, clean, and easy to read.

87
00:03:37,083 --> 00:03:39,720
Tap an answer, save and next.

88
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:43,160
Now she switches to another app — and the exam catches

89
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:43,560
it.

90
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,160
Warning one of three.

91
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:46,597
Straight back to the paper.

92
00:03:46,697 --> 00:03:48,537
Let's fast-forward to the end.

93
00:03:48,537 --> 00:03:50,110
Submit, and confirm.

94
00:03:50,666 --> 00:03:53,582
Number nine: watch the exam live.

95
00:03:54,262 --> 00:03:57,222
Back on your dashboard: thirty students writing right

96
00:03:57,222 --> 00:03:59,302
now, two already submitted.

97
00:03:59,302 --> 00:04:02,502
Open Results — started, writing, submitted,

98
00:04:02,502 --> 00:04:03,302
dropped.

99
00:04:03,302 --> 00:04:06,742
Tap any tile to see exactly who, and how far they've

100
00:04:06,742 --> 00:04:07,209
got.

101
00:04:07,748 --> 00:04:11,058
And number ten: results, the moment they submit.

102
00:04:11,738 --> 00:04:14,858
She sees her score instantly — seventy-five percent

103
00:04:14,858 --> 00:04:17,137
with the solution key, if you allow it.

104
00:04:17,872 --> 00:04:20,752
And when everyone's done, all thirty-two results are

105
00:04:20,752 --> 00:04:21,232
in.

106
00:04:21,232 --> 00:04:23,632
Turn on ranks, scroll the whole batch,

107
00:04:23,632 --> 00:04:26,338
and download everything to Excel, in one click.

108
00:04:27,192 --> 00:04:30,392
That's ten features — from a question paper to ranked

109
00:04:30,392 --> 00:04:32,472
results, all in one place.

110
00:04:32,472 --> 00:04:35,790
Try it at testoza dot com, and subscribe for more.
